You enter the adyton to see the Pythia, the Oracle of Delphi. Normal members of the general public would not be permitted to enter the adyton, but you're a time traveler. You are from the future yourself, so the Pythia allows you to bear witness to her visions of the future. She is sitting atop her tripod seat over a chasm in the floor. She inhales the vapors filling the room and speaks her prophecy to you:

You have traveled long and hard,
From far away in the distant hereafter.
You seek to gain knowledge of centuries past,
As you hunt for your stone prize.

Go now to the great city of Athena!
Seek out the Erechtheion,
And find the punished women,
Cursed are they to hold up the King's ceiling!